  "narration": {
    "title": "Schwarber Sets the Home Run Pace at 43",
    "intro": "It's a hitting day, and the top of the board belongs to power and patience. Kyle Schwarber leads the home run race at 43, Yordan Alvarez is on a historic run, and the Cubs quietly own the best lineup in the game. Elly De La Cruz reminded everyone he can still change a scoreboard in a hurry.",
    "offense_lead": "The Cubs sit atop the team-OPS board at .769, a step clear of the Dodgers at .755, with Washington close behind at .752. The Rockies sneaking into the top five at .739 is the small surprise here.",
    "bats_lead": "Yordan Alvarez headlines the elite bats at a 1.021 OPS on a historic pace, though it cooled a touch this week. Pete Crow-Armstrong keeps climbing behind him at .949 and now 41 homers, the rare Cub doing damage every way you count it.",
    "season_leaders_lead": "Luis Arraez owns the batting title chase at .316, just ahead of Alvarez at .311, while Sal Stewart leads the RBI race with 107. It's a spread-out leaderboard, with three different Rays sitting inside the top five in average.",
    "hr_lead": "Kyle Schwarber leads all hitters with 43, adding three in a weekend series against Atlanta, with Crow-Armstrong right behind at 41. Elly De La Cruz was the week's real mover, four homers over four straight days against Milwaukee and the Dodgers, while Rafael Devers matched him with a two-homer night in New York."
  }
